# Markdown twins (<page>.md, from src/pages/**/*.md.ts): consolidated into their
# HTML page by an HTTP canonical (no noindex: Google reads noindex + canonical as
# conflicting signals; AI crawlers still read the twin), and without the font preloads
# of /* (the "! Link" drops those; the canonical Link is set after it). Cloudflare
# Pages docs (pages/configuration/headers): a splat "*" greedily matches any
# characters, one per rule, and may sit mid-pattern ("/*.jpg"); its match is
# reused in a value as ":splat". One rule per twin section, not "/*.md": the
# /templates/*.md downloads are not twins and have no HTML page to point at.
# tests/seo-md-twins.spec.ts replays these rules on dist to prove that every twin
# and no HTML page matches.
/bok/*.md
  ! Link
  Link: <https://aigovernanceengineer.com/bok/:splat>; rel="canonical"
/patterns/*.md
  ! Link
  Link: <https://aigovernanceengineer.com/patterns/:splat>; rel="canonical"
/cases/*.md
  ! Link
  Link: <https://aigovernanceengineer.com/cases/:splat>; rel="canonical"
/glossary/*.md
  ! Link
  Link: <https://aigovernanceengineer.com/glossary/:splat>; rel="canonical"
/thesis.md
  ! Link
  Link: <https://aigovernanceengineer.com/thesis>; rel="canonical"
/ai-governance.md
  ! Link
  Link: <https://aigovernanceengineer.com/ai-governance>; rel="canonical"
/llms*
